                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c0d1a6ea-3827-4b76-8697-144d232ed9a5",
                        "entry_id": "3a30640f-3213-3127-8555-e62f8ecdc380",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hachettes"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e54742d2-3f9a-46cd-92e5-32eb820a3665",
                        "entry_id": "3a30640f-3213-3127-8555-e62f8ecdc380",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "^((h aspiré))\\a.ʃɛt\\"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "38147448-cf53-3a26-bd57-d94a42489633",
                        "entry_id": "3a30640f-3213-3127-8555-e62f8ecdc380",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petite hache."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "356f44b1-14f4-40a3-80ba-9081f58df556",
                                "sense_id": "38147448-cf53-3a26-bd57-d94a42489633",
                                "text": "En outre, le lieutenant et le sous-officier portaient la hachette et le couteau à neige, qui n’abandonnent jamais un voyageur des régions polaires."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "efc299f4-a3c9-477d-b3a5-1badda52bec3",
                                "sense_id": "38147448-cf53-3a26-bd57-d94a42489633",
                                "text": "Les enquêteurs ont fini par retrouver à Hong Kong la trace de ce contrôleur aérien français soupçonné d’avoir assassiné à la hachette l’un de ses collègues au sein même de la tour de contrôle de l’aéroport Bâle-Mulhouse-Fribourg, en avril 2011, avant d’organiser sa disparition en mettant la police sur une série de fausse piste."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "50c74a35-64b6-3857-854e-3f0a83175c7b",
                        "entry_id": "3a30640f-3213-3127-8555-e62f8ecdc380",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Espèce d’insecte lépidoptère (papillon) nocturne de la famille des saturnidés (Saturnidae) dont le dos des ailes est de couleur brun-sable avec une ocelle sur chaque aile."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Lépidoptérologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fe29a98-1df6-41ae-af56-3f9dca610ced",
                                "sense_id": "50c74a35-64b6-3857-854e-3f0a83175c7b",
                                "text": "La chenille de la hachette se nourrit sur des frênes, des chênes, des bouleaux, etc."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5a4b3715-194f-3e45-8057-b4a8c2a30075",
                        "entry_id": "3a30640f-3213-3127-8555-e62f8ecdc380",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Plante fourragère, genre Securigera."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d28b15f4-68bd-4fab-9811-e6006921f5a4",
                                "sense_id": "5a4b3715-194f-3e45-8057-b4a8c2a30075",
                                "text": "8. La Serradelle commune est l’Ornithopus sativus, à côté duquel il faut citer comme plantes fourragères les Coronilla varia L., Emerus L., les Râteaux (Biserrula), les Pieds-d’oiseau (Ornithopus), les Fers-à-cheval (Hippocrepis), les Chenillons (Scorpiurus) et les Hachettes (Securigera), tous si remarquables par la forme de leurs fruits. (Voy. pp. 281, 292, 293, 309, 310, et Rosenth., op. cit., 1009, 1010.)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "988879f0-939c-496c-832f-96a810046e8a",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a30640f-3213-3127-8555-e62f8ecdc380",
                        "source_sense_description": "Petite hache",
                        "target_lang_word": "hatchet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hatchet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a0b7b30-aa54-38f9-9ee5-c79b356b1af7",
                                        "entry_id": "c8975c12-9eff-32eb-99eb-eb23941e5c42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small, light axe with a short handle; a tomahawk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "472be60b-8e0f-4e8a-a5da-568bfea421a5",
                                                "sense_id": "5a0b7b30-aa54-38f9-9ee5-c79b356b1af7",
                                                "text": "“It must be admitted, Nick, you are a very literal logician—‘dog won't eat dog,’ is our English saying. Still the Yankee will fight the Yengeese, it would seem. In a word, the Great Father, in England, has raised the hatchet against his American children.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "202e0aa5-00fb-46d2-b1c9-7d5f517266d8",
                                                "sense_id": "5a0b7b30-aa54-38f9-9ee5-c79b356b1af7",
                                                "text": "Buried was the bloody hatchet, / Buried was the dreadful war-club, / Buried were all warlike weapons, / And the war-cry was forgotten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "557d3c9b-d0e0-4b05-960d-58b56fb9b86b",
                                                "sense_id": "5a0b7b30-aa54-38f9-9ee5-c79b356b1af7",
                                                "text": "The fellow was armed with a stone-shod spear, a stone knife and a hatchet. In his black hair were several gay-colored feathers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac101717-44c1-3df5-9537-e2d19c068b72",
                                        "entry_id": "c8975c12-9eff-32eb-99eb-eb23941e5c42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Belligerence, animosity; harsh criticism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0760f77-e07b-4b60-8312-2b20007c8083",
                                                "sense_id": "ac101717-44c1-3df5-9537-e2d19c068b72",
                                                "text": "to bury the hatchet"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bdf2576-11f9-4fdc-8a9d-c08822ebf61c",
                                                "sense_id": "ac101717-44c1-3df5-9537-e2d19c068b72",
                                                "text": "hatchet job"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b86c702-a75f-4824-8335-641ceb7a98b3",
                                                "sense_id": "ac101717-44c1-3df5-9537-e2d19c068b72",
                                                "text": "“Dat true as missionary! What a soldier do, cap'in, if so much peace? Warrior love a war-path.”\n“I wish it were not so, Nick. But my hatchet is buried, I hope, for ever.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71dd976e-cac2-42e8-8047-b1bd9be17b97",
                                                "sense_id": "ac101717-44c1-3df5-9537-e2d19c068b72",
                                                "text": "The savagery with which Michael Hofmann can wield a hatchet has earned him unlikely fans outside the literary circuit. A recent issue of Viz ran a cartoon of the critic, poet and translator urinating all over a phone booth, while two donnish FR Leavis types nodded appreciatively from a safe distance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hatchet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "baab1498-d969-33b6-9fe9-739b1b4711ad",
                                        "entry_id": "315163f6-1246-32a1-b85b-bb10ab7f2f12",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut with a hatchet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
